      "Status": "warn",
      "Evidence": "There are strong seductive textures scattered throughout (the fold\u0027s \u0027heartbeat of warm gold with no up and no edges,\u0027 the Sentinel as \u0027an altar built to worship the thing it guarded,\u0027 the lens \u0027weeping something slow and amber, warm as bread from an oven\u0027), but these are frequently interrupted by long stretches of procedural/expository material (the boot-print deduction, checkpoint logistics, institutional history recitation) that reads as observation rather than allure, diluting the pull before horror lands.",
      "Fix": "Trim the investigative and expository passages (boot-print analysis, Relic provenance lectures, institutional history) so the strange-beautiful sensory details carry more of the narrative weight relative to procedural exposition."
    },
